WEBVTT

00:13.513 --> 00:14.973
I have obtained a disc.

00:15.056 --> 00:16.057
Just one of them.

00:16.141 --> 00:17.892
We can bring him back.

00:17.976 --> 00:20.937
I just know that
the discs will bring him back.

00:21.021 --> 00:24.649
Let's call it
Operation Savage Guardian for now.

00:25.316 --> 00:26.818
You should take him.

00:26.901 --> 00:28.403
He can aid your cause.

00:28.987 --> 00:32.323
His name is Weather Forecast.

00:33.116 --> 00:34.492
Jumpin' Jack Spark!

00:34.576 --> 00:36.411
Weather Forecast!

00:42.959 --> 00:45.628
But where did he go?

00:46.129 --> 00:48.048
I need to get the disc back!

02:19.889 --> 02:22.016
EPISODE 11: OPERATION SAVAGE GUARDIAN
(HEAD TO THE COURTYARD!) (2)

02:22.100 --> 02:23.977
Emergency alarm activated.

02:24.060 --> 02:25.395
Corridor 7B.

02:25.979 --> 02:28.606
-Yes, that's correct. Corridor 7B.
-Emergency alarm activated.

02:28.690 --> 02:30.483
We are awaiting reports.

02:30.567 --> 02:31.985
Did something happen?

02:32.068 --> 02:33.361
We aren't sure as of yet.

02:33.444 --> 02:37.824
But Corridor 7B's sole function
is for access to the factory.

02:37.907 --> 02:41.286
There is no possibility
that it is a fire or a prisoner riot.

02:41.369 --> 02:42.537
Rest assured.

02:42.620 --> 02:44.497
Yes, indeed.

02:45.081 --> 02:48.751
I trust this prison and the prisoners.

02:49.419 --> 02:53.590
With all the commotion,
curiosity got the better of me.

02:54.174 --> 02:56.259
Surely, you are aware

02:56.342 --> 02:59.804
that no prisoner has managed
to escape from this prison for 20 years.

03:00.471 --> 03:02.932
Furthermore, the courtyard
is outside of Corridor 7B.

03:03.016 --> 03:06.019
No prisoner would choose
to escape from there, of all places.

03:07.270 --> 03:08.855
You're quite right.

03:08.938 --> 03:10.481
Leave the rest to us, Father.

03:10.565 --> 03:11.900
I'll be off then.

03:18.990 --> 03:21.326
Just one more thing out of curiosity…

03:22.285 --> 03:24.621
Is the clock on the wall accurate?

03:25.705 --> 03:26.998
Yes, of course.

03:27.081 --> 03:29.751
It is now 11:58 a.m.

03:29.834 --> 03:31.419
It's almost lunchtime.

03:35.924 --> 03:37.967
11:51 a.m.

03:38.051 --> 03:40.428
 A call to The Speedwagon Foundation.

03:42.805 --> 03:44.474
I have the usual request.

03:45.058 --> 03:49.646
I'd like access to the collect call list
and the recorded conversations.

03:50.271 --> 03:52.815
Women's prison, phone booth 16.

03:53.483 --> 03:55.860
The call from about seven minutes ago.

03:56.861 --> 03:58.404
Weather Forecast.

03:59.072 --> 04:00.740
Since you touched me,

04:00.823 --> 04:03.368
you are now weightless too.

04:08.623 --> 04:10.500
I don't see our enemy anywhere.

04:10.583 --> 04:12.585
We need to retrieve the disc right away.

04:13.544 --> 04:14.796
Stay calm.

04:15.463 --> 04:18.299
He must be within this laundry room.

04:18.383 --> 04:19.592
He is lurking somewhere.

04:21.052 --> 04:23.388
The courtyard is past that door.

04:24.138 --> 04:26.182
You are trying to reach that door,

04:27.100 --> 04:29.352
but it is most likely locked.

04:29.435 --> 04:32.772
You might need to blast it,
or force it open somehow.

04:34.524 --> 04:37.068
There's... A slight problem...

04:38.486 --> 04:41.447
I know now's not the time for this…

04:41.531 --> 04:43.574
It's a personal thing…

04:43.658 --> 04:46.619
But it's urgent, and I need to go now.

04:47.245 --> 04:48.830
So, like…

04:49.622 --> 04:52.417
I don't know why it suddenly so suddenly.

04:52.500 --> 04:54.294
But, well…

04:54.377 --> 04:56.546
It's something that happens to everyone!

04:58.047 --> 04:59.549
What is this about?

04:59.632 --> 05:00.758
Well,

05:00.842 --> 05:04.095
it's the P-word related to
the pelvic area.

05:04.178 --> 05:06.973
I'm just glad it's not "number two."

05:07.056 --> 05:08.891
You know, the biological phenomenon!

05:09.934 --> 05:11.311
You need to take a piss?

05:11.394 --> 05:13.271
No need to say it up close.

05:13.938 --> 05:15.898
I'm serious. I need to go.

05:18.443 --> 05:20.111
Just pick any corner.

05:20.194 --> 05:25.074
Dammit, why did I even try
talking to a guy about this?

05:25.158 --> 05:27.035
I have relieved myself already.

05:27.118 --> 05:29.203
See? It's floating over there.

05:30.830 --> 05:35.793
In zero gravity, the blood in your body
will suddenly collect in your head.

05:36.294 --> 05:40.298
Blood that is usually in the lower parts
of the body due to gravity.

05:40.882 --> 05:45.053
The space between the skin and the bone
is swollen and squishy with blood.

05:45.136 --> 05:46.888
It's called a "moon face."

05:49.098 --> 05:50.099
However,

05:50.183 --> 05:53.353
it's dangerous when too much blood
goes to your head.

05:53.436 --> 05:57.732
The kidney automatically works harder
to reduce the amount of blood.

05:58.316 --> 06:00.735
This triggers an acute diuretic effect.

06:01.277 --> 06:03.237
It attempts to thin the blood content

06:03.321 --> 06:05.073
by expelling salt.

06:05.156 --> 06:07.200
-But--
-Don't worry.

06:07.283 --> 06:09.285
I'll use my clouds to absorb your urine.

06:09.369 --> 06:10.244
What?

06:13.623 --> 06:17.418
Hey, wait, what are these droplets?

06:17.502 --> 06:19.587
They're leaking out of your cloud!

06:30.848 --> 06:32.350
Weather Forecast!

06:32.433 --> 06:33.935
No, that's not it.

06:34.018 --> 06:36.437
It's being sucked out
through the gap in the wall!

06:36.521 --> 06:37.730
Me too.

06:37.814 --> 06:39.565
Blood from the wound I got earlier.

06:40.149 --> 06:42.443
My nose won't stop bleeding!

06:42.527 --> 06:46.406
I'm having difficulty breathing…

06:46.489 --> 06:48.241
No, it can't be!

06:50.993 --> 06:51.828
Jolyne!

07:00.837 --> 07:04.006
Everything I touch becomes zero gravity.

07:05.550 --> 07:09.178
I touched the walls leading to the door.

07:10.513 --> 07:13.641
That means the whole room
is unaffected by gravity!

07:15.017 --> 07:15.852
The air!

07:15.935 --> 07:18.813
Air can't stay in zero gravity!

07:18.896 --> 07:21.691
It'll get pulled by
the surrounding gravity, and it'll escape!

07:23.109 --> 07:25.278
We need to close up the gap!

07:25.361 --> 07:28.781
Otherwise, we'll suffocate to death!

07:28.865 --> 07:30.032
Jolyne, you're wrong.

07:30.116 --> 07:32.034
Suffocation isn't our primary concern.

07:32.118 --> 07:36.789
The blood in our bodies will boil first,
leading to our death.

07:37.290 --> 07:41.586
In a vacuum, blood boils up like water.

07:41.669 --> 07:43.546
In a zero-gravity vacuum,

07:43.629 --> 07:46.215
people's blood will dry up in 20 seconds,

07:46.299 --> 07:49.177
before even suffocating.

08:00.980 --> 08:03.608
I'll reload my bullets.

08:06.277 --> 08:07.361
We'll get shot.

08:07.945 --> 08:10.239
We must hide somewhere!

08:10.323 --> 08:11.657
What are you saying?

08:11.741 --> 08:13.326
I'm bleeding out of my nose!

08:13.409 --> 08:15.119
We need to stop the air!

08:15.745 --> 08:16.787
Weather Forecast!

08:46.526 --> 08:48.736
Just take shallow breaths.

08:49.320 --> 08:52.031
I gathered what little air
is remaining in this room,

08:52.615 --> 08:55.243
and covered our bodies with clouds.

08:57.578 --> 08:59.372
Cloud suits.

09:00.706 --> 09:02.708
The room is almost a complete vacuum.

09:02.792 --> 09:05.586
This is all the remaining air.

09:06.504 --> 09:08.214
Your nosebleed has stopped.

09:09.423 --> 09:12.552
How long can we keep breathing?

09:13.219 --> 09:15.221
I wish I didn't have to answer that.

09:15.304 --> 09:17.682
I'd say about two minutes.

09:17.765 --> 09:19.767
It's a cloud suit on the verge of death.

09:20.309 --> 09:22.687
If we don't defeat our enemy
within that time,

09:23.271 --> 09:26.107
we'll be thrown into the vacuum, right?

09:27.066 --> 09:28.317
Precisely.

09:30.486 --> 09:31.737
Where is he?

09:32.738 --> 09:33.948
We must find him.

09:34.031 --> 09:35.825
Whether we act or not,

09:36.409 --> 09:38.661
his attack will finish us both.

09:39.161 --> 09:41.831
Hey, now that my nosebleed has stopped,

09:41.914 --> 09:43.541
I notice something.

09:43.624 --> 09:44.834
Listen, Jolyne.

09:44.917 --> 09:47.378
I said two minutes, but it could be one!

09:47.461 --> 09:49.338
We must find him immediately!

09:49.422 --> 09:51.340
Carbon dioxide is increasing as we speak!

09:51.924 --> 09:53.009
The laundry hampers.

09:53.509 --> 09:55.136
They aren't floating.

09:56.095 --> 09:57.847
The hampers over there.

09:58.639 --> 10:02.184
I touched the walls, shutters,
and floor of this room.

10:02.268 --> 10:04.895
That's why the whole room
entered zero gravity,

10:04.979 --> 10:06.564
and everything is floating.

10:07.732 --> 10:11.402
But why are those hampers
and barrels not floating,

10:11.485 --> 10:12.987
and attached to the floor?

10:14.322 --> 10:16.073
Also, that enemy.

10:16.866 --> 10:20.745
How is he breathing in a vacuum?

10:20.828 --> 10:23.831
Shouldn't his blood be boiling over?

10:27.585 --> 10:28.502
In other words,

10:29.920 --> 10:31.922
that's the range of his ability.

10:33.049 --> 10:35.384
There is a distance range
to this zero gravity.

10:36.135 --> 10:38.220
It's not the entire room!

10:38.304 --> 10:39.764
An attack range!

10:40.264 --> 10:41.932
From here to the hampers

10:42.642 --> 10:44.310
is about 20 meters or so.

10:44.393 --> 10:46.354
Zero gravity ends there.

10:46.437 --> 10:49.607
If we can get there,
there will surely be normal air!

10:50.191 --> 10:52.443
You must go, Weather Forecast.

10:52.526 --> 10:54.236
He is outside of the vacuum range.

10:54.320 --> 10:56.906
If you do not control the air now,

10:56.989 --> 10:59.158
we will never reach our enemy.

11:00.034 --> 11:01.911
You may be correct.

11:01.994 --> 11:03.621
Outside that hamper…

11:10.127 --> 11:12.046
Go, Weather Forecast.

11:12.129 --> 11:15.007
The pressure in the suit
is becoming strange.

11:15.091 --> 11:18.594
Go before this cloud suit
disperses into the vacuum!

11:36.696 --> 11:39.407
Don't think you can
get out of my attack range!

11:39.490 --> 11:40.700
He's gonna shoot him down!

11:41.492 --> 11:42.535
I won't let you!

11:43.828 --> 11:46.455
I'll protect Weather Forecast!

11:51.085 --> 11:52.962
STAND NAME: WEATHER FORECAST
STAND MASTER: WEATHER FORECAST

11:54.797 --> 11:56.298
He's coming around us!

11:56.382 --> 11:57.800
I'll charge ahead!

12:32.293 --> 12:35.463
He's going to reach air in a few meters.

12:35.546 --> 12:38.215
Once Weather Forecast gets air,

12:38.299 --> 12:39.967
he's going to corner you!

12:40.050 --> 12:43.095
If you want air that bad, you can have it.

12:43.679 --> 12:46.015
No need to even reach the hampers.

12:46.724 --> 12:48.058
I just now

12:48.768 --> 12:51.020
completed my attack.

12:52.938 --> 12:57.485
I wasn't trying to ricochet
the bullets to injure him.

12:57.985 --> 13:00.196
I shot the barrel itself!

13:03.449 --> 13:06.118
A bit of air is left in the barrel.

13:06.202 --> 13:08.954
Highly pressurized air

13:09.038 --> 13:11.582
on the verge of explosion, that is!

13:14.543 --> 13:15.544
Weather Forecast!

13:24.011 --> 13:26.764
He was pushed back to zero gravity.

13:26.847 --> 13:28.891
He is done for.

13:29.850 --> 13:34.480
He won't be able to gain enough force
to stop the momentum.

13:36.023 --> 13:37.900
Weather Forecast!

13:37.983 --> 13:38.859
This is it.

13:38.943 --> 13:41.862
The suit itself is about to collapse!

13:50.746 --> 13:53.040
Jolyne! How reckless!

13:53.123 --> 13:54.416
You must go back!

13:54.500 --> 13:55.709
He'll shoot you down!

13:55.793 --> 13:59.088
That thrust itself
will dissipate your suit!

13:59.672 --> 14:01.841
She makes incredibly quick decisions.

14:02.591 --> 14:05.803
She charged into that bastard
to stop his movement,

14:06.595 --> 14:10.349
and to push him outside of
the zero gravity again!

14:12.142 --> 14:13.269
However,

14:14.270 --> 14:16.146
I won't let you through!

14:18.774 --> 14:20.484
I already know.

14:20.568 --> 14:22.736
Your Stand is very powerful.

14:23.404 --> 14:28.576
My rotating bullets aren't fast enough,
and would get flicked away in defense.

14:29.159 --> 14:30.953
That's why I've been preparing.

14:31.495 --> 14:32.580
I've looked for them.

14:33.247 --> 14:35.708
I'd captured them away from view.

14:38.335 --> 14:39.670
There were quite a lot.

14:39.753 --> 14:41.630
Rats! They're alive!

14:42.673 --> 14:44.550
Could they be…

14:45.134 --> 14:46.010
Stone Ocean!

14:46.093 --> 14:47.928
Push them away!

14:51.932 --> 14:52.892
I can't see!

14:53.392 --> 14:54.226
Okay!

14:54.768 --> 14:58.606
I did not expect you to fight
against my ability like this.

14:59.189 --> 15:00.608
This is checkmate.

15:01.108 --> 15:03.986
You're finished, Jolyne Cujoh!

15:06.405 --> 15:08.908
My mission is now complete!

15:15.831 --> 15:18.667
Jumpin' Jack Spark is the best.

15:19.251 --> 15:21.462
I feel invincible.

15:21.545 --> 15:23.589
I'm glad I was imprisoned here.

15:24.089 --> 15:26.342
With this ability I obtained here,

15:26.425 --> 15:29.011
there is nothing I can't do in this world.

15:29.511 --> 15:31.680
My future is rosy!

15:32.389 --> 15:34.892
I will hand this disc over to Pale Snake.

15:35.476 --> 15:38.020
I can defeat him too, if I wanted to.

15:38.687 --> 15:40.564
WIth my own hands!

15:54.995 --> 15:56.163
I knew it…

15:58.791 --> 16:02.211
I knew you'd do it.

16:02.294 --> 16:03.879
I was waiting

16:04.380 --> 16:05.547
for you to reload.

16:05.631 --> 16:07.925
I was waiting with my threads ready

16:08.008 --> 16:10.052
for you to reload your gun.

16:10.135 --> 16:12.554
And you shot at me.

16:13.472 --> 16:14.306
These threads!

16:14.390 --> 16:16.308
When the hell did you do this?!

16:16.392 --> 16:17.977
Stone Ocean!

16:22.523 --> 16:25.567
What?

16:33.033 --> 16:36.370
You are the one in a complete vacuum.

16:36.453 --> 16:37.746
And now,

16:37.830 --> 16:40.916
without a suit, your blood will boil up

16:41.000 --> 16:42.793
and explode faster than us!

16:45.671 --> 16:46.714
We won!

16:46.797 --> 16:48.215
If you don't want to die,

16:48.298 --> 16:51.635
you must deactivate
the zero gravity immediately!

16:54.471 --> 16:55.597
Dammit!

16:58.225 --> 17:00.686
The crime that put me in this prison…

17:01.186 --> 17:04.231
How many times did I stab her?

17:04.815 --> 17:07.735
When I killed the female professor,

17:07.818 --> 17:10.946
the prosecutor said
I stabbed her 69 times.

17:11.864 --> 17:13.407
That compulsion.

17:13.490 --> 17:15.325
It's surging within me once more.

17:15.951 --> 17:17.036
Shit.

17:17.119 --> 17:19.079
I won't let you underestimate me.

17:19.163 --> 17:20.539
That bitch!

17:22.416 --> 17:25.377
A reaction between hydrogen peroxide
and manganese dioxide

17:25.461 --> 17:27.963
produces oxygen.

17:28.547 --> 17:32.676
Just like the oxygen in this bottle,
it keeps coming out!

17:33.719 --> 17:38.724
My urge to slaughter someone
like back then!

17:38.807 --> 17:39.683
Take this!

17:39.767 --> 17:45.064
I'll make a headstone out of
your piss-soaked body with this glass!

17:55.866 --> 17:59.328
Jolyne Cujoh,
your blood vessels will rupture first

17:59.411 --> 18:01.914
since you are covered in wounds!

18:01.997 --> 18:04.249
I got incarcerated for murder.

18:04.333 --> 18:09.046
I will kill you
and leave this place an invincible man!

18:17.763 --> 18:19.223
Take this.

18:19.306 --> 18:20.474
This will be sufficient

18:20.557 --> 18:23.227
just to take the disc back

18:24.561 --> 18:27.564
from that bastard.

18:29.525 --> 18:31.026
Weather Forecast!

18:31.610 --> 18:33.529
What?

18:33.612 --> 18:36.990
Dammit! My body is at its limit!

18:37.574 --> 18:40.452
If I deactivate my ability,
the air will rush in.

18:41.161 --> 18:43.539
I may be able to escape using the impact!

18:44.373 --> 18:46.667
Zero gravity, deactivate!

18:46.750 --> 18:49.878
Jumpin' Jack Spark!

19:01.014 --> 19:03.851
You should've deactivated it
the first chance you had.

19:03.934 --> 19:07.104
The change in air pressure
might have let you escape.

19:07.688 --> 19:11.817
If only you had deactivated it while
you still had distance from Stone Ocean.

19:11.900 --> 19:17.281
The air is blowing you back toward me!

19:41.096 --> 19:44.808
How much longer
until The Speedwagon Foundation arrives?

19:44.892 --> 19:46.977
Three minutes? Or two minutes?

19:48.228 --> 19:50.981
There is a corridor past this door.

19:51.565 --> 19:55.694
Alongside the right wall, there are
windows that look out to the courtyard.

19:55.777 --> 19:59.239
There, you'll be able to see
a revolving door's gate.

19:59.323 --> 20:01.325
This gate leads to the courtyard.

20:02.659 --> 20:06.830
The gate is accessible
during the day and is unlocked.

20:07.497 --> 20:11.585
The next challenge
is how to go about opening this door.

20:11.668 --> 20:13.545
I'll get a prison guard to open it.

20:14.254 --> 20:16.381
We have his work permit.

20:17.674 --> 20:19.426
We'll trick them into opening it.

20:20.552 --> 20:22.012
I see.

20:22.095 --> 20:24.806
Once the door opens,
you'll knock the guards out

20:24.890 --> 20:27.559
and force your way to the courtyard.

20:28.227 --> 20:29.269
Very well.

20:30.062 --> 20:33.023
Not only will you be charged
with attempted escape,

20:33.106 --> 20:36.026
but you'll also receive
solitary confinement for six months

20:36.109 --> 20:39.279
where you cannot even
exercise sufficiently.

20:40.197 --> 20:41.281
That's fine.

20:42.157 --> 20:43.784
I'll go to the courtyard

20:43.867 --> 20:46.495
and hand this disc over to someone
from The Speedwagon Foundation.

20:47.621 --> 20:51.583
That's my only mission in life right now.

20:59.967 --> 21:01.093
The guards are coming.

21:01.677 --> 21:04.513
Weather Forecast,
go find somewhere to hide.

21:05.013 --> 21:07.015
I'll go by myself from here.

21:07.099 --> 21:08.934
You're severely wounded,

21:09.017 --> 21:11.436
and if the guards see your injury,

21:11.520 --> 21:13.021
they might lock the gate.

21:13.105 --> 21:14.815
Very well. I understand.

21:20.279 --> 21:21.571
What is it?

21:22.197 --> 21:23.615
Why are you knocking?

21:28.120 --> 21:29.121
It's you.

21:29.871 --> 21:31.248
"It's you"?

21:32.416 --> 21:34.418
What is it, Rangler?

21:34.501 --> 21:36.169
What is this noise about?

21:36.253 --> 21:38.213
Hold still. I'll open the door.

21:44.678 --> 21:46.513
If you are returning to the men's prison,

21:47.014 --> 21:50.726
Lang Rangler, how about we stop
by the chapel on the way?

21:51.601 --> 21:53.270
I'd like to speak to you.

21:55.605 --> 21:56.732
It's not a guard!

22:05.866 --> 22:07.367
Who is he?

22:07.909 --> 22:10.370
He's neither a guard nor a prisoner!

22:11.913 --> 22:14.750
What could his attire mean?

23:41.002 --> 23:46.007
Subtitle translation by: Megumi Hunter
